            <ArticleTitle>Using quantitative acid-base analysis in the ICU.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>19-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The quantitative acid-base 'Strong Ion' calculator is a practical application of quantitative acid-base chemistry, as developed by Peter Stewart and Peter Constable. It quantifies the three independent factors that control acidity, calculates the concentration and charge of unmeasured ions, produces a report based on these calculations and displays a Gamblegram depicting measured ionic species. Used together with the medical history, quantitative acid-base analysis has advantages over traditional approaches.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
